<p>
A prayer for the First Sunday of Lent:
</p>

<p>
Father,
</p>

<p>
The dying tree,<br>
desperate to stay alive,<br>
tries to maintain<br>
the illusion of being<br>
healthy and full,<br>
but it cannot<br>
hide the truth,<br>
for it saps life from<br>
everything around it.
</p>

<p>
Forgive me,<br>
for I take much<br>
more than I give,<br>
and like the tree,<br>
never truly live.
</p>

<p>
May these roots<br>
once again taste<br>
the goodness of<br>
your grace, and<br>
these branches<br>
be a blessing<br>
to all that<br>
I encounter.
</p>

<p>
<i>Amen</i>
</p>


